{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>I am Pharaoh, and besides you.</b> It is a parable — only the throne is greater than you; but he needed to repeat and write it at the time of giving the ring." "<b>No man shall lift his hand.</b> To assume authority, as written concerning Jeroboam who lifted a hand against the king — he lifted his hand and his authority over King Solomon, as stated: ויפקידהו לכל סבל בית יוסף."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The word רק is read as modifying the throne's superiority; the sentence is terse and slightly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:18.125961947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}